  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FN8">Lemma <span data-tag="0FN8">4.43.14</span>.</a> Let $(\mathcal{C}, \otimes , \phi , \psi )$ be a symmetric monoidal category. Let $X$ be an object of $\mathcal{C}$ and let $Y$, $\eta : \mathbf{1} \to X \otimes Y$, and $\epsilon : Y \otimes X \to \mathbf{1}$ be a left dual of $X$ as in Definition <a href="/tag/0FFP" data-tag="0FFP">4.43.8</a>. Then $\eta ' = \psi \circ \eta : \mathbf{1} \to Y \otimes X$ and $\epsilon ' = \epsilon \circ \psi : X \otimes Y \to \mathbf{1}$ makes $X$ into a left dual of $Y$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
